    body: "<table>\n      <tr><td>Version</td><td>1.0 (for issue)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Date</td><td>28 August 2026</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Owner</td><td>Chief Executive Officer</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Applies to</td><td>Every person issued a contract of employment or an engagement letter</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Status</td><td>Issued with the contract. <strong>The signed schedule at section 5 forms part of the contract.</strong></td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Review</td><td>On any change to an annexed document</td></tr>\n    </table>\n    <h2>1 &nbsp;What you have been given</h2>\n    <p>Your contract of employment sets out your role, pay, hours, leave and notice. It does not repeat the standards of conduct, clinical limits and information-handling rules that apply to everyone. Those sit in the documents listed below, which are incorporated into your contract by reference. Read them before you sign.</p>\n    <p>Where a document says an obligation continues after your engagement ends, it does. Confidentiality and the restricted periods in the Code of Conduct are the principal examples.</p>\n    <h2>2 &nbsp;The annexes</h2>\n    <table>\n      <tr>\n        <td>A</td>\n        <td><strong>Code of Conduct</strong><br><span>v1.0, 26 August 2026</span></td>\n        <td>The standards expected of everyone, and the conduct that ends an engagement. Contains the gift rule, the substances rule, and the restricted periods that apply after you leave.</td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr>\n        <td>B</td>\n        <td><strong>Confidentiality Policy</strong><br><span>v1.0, 26 August 2026</span></td>\n        <td>What you may and may not say about a client, to whom, and when. These obligations survive the end of your engagement without time limit.</td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr>\n        <td>C</td>\n        <td><strong>Data Protection and Information Handling</strong><br><span>Employee edition, v1.0, 28 August 2026</span></td>\n        <td>How records, devices and messages are handled under the Nigeria Data Protection Act 2023. Section 4 contains the rules you are agreeing to; section 6 tells you what to do if something is lost or sent to the wrong person.</td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr>\n        <td>D</td>\n        <td><strong>Scope of Practice Policy</strong><br><span>v1.2, 28 August 2026</span></td>\n        <td>What your cadre may and may not do, and the medication levels. Applies to clinical and care roles. Issued to non-clinical staff for information, since it governs the work they support.</td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr>\n        <td>E</td>\n        <td><strong>Disciplinary and Grievance Procedure</strong><br><span>v1.0, 26 August 2026</span></td>\n        <td>How concerns about your conduct are handled, and how you raise a concern of your own. Part B is not binding as to procedure, so Medic Connect may adapt the steps to the circumstances.</td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr>\n        <td>F</td>\n        <td><strong>Job description</strong><br><span>Role-specific</span></td>\n        <td>Your duties, reporting line and how performance is measured. Descriptive rather than exhaustive, and may be varied on reasonable notice.</td>\n      </tr>\n    </table>\n    <h2>3 &nbsp;How the documents fit together</h2>\n    <p><strong>3.1 The contract governs.</strong> Where the contract of employment and an annex conflict on pay, hours, leave or notice, the contract prevails. Where they conflict on conduct, clinical limits or information handling, the annex prevails.</p>\n    <p><strong>3.2 Amendment.</strong> Annexes are reviewed annually and may be amended. Material changes are notified in writing and take effect from the date stated. Continuing to work after that date is acceptance of the amended document.</p>\n    <p><strong>3.3 Non-employees.</strong> Where you are engaged on shift or placement work rather than employed, the same annexes apply, and references to disciplinary action are read as the roster provisions at Part C of the Disciplinary and Grievance Procedure.</p>\n    <p><strong>3.4 Copies.</strong> A copy of each annex is issued with your contract and held on your file. A further copy is available from your line manager on request at any time.</p>\n    <h2>4 &nbsp;Before you sign</h2>\n    <div>\n      <div>Do not sign the schedule below until you have read all six documents and had any question answered. If anything is unclear, ask before signing rather than after.</div>\n    </div>\n    <p>Three provisions carry consequences beyond the end of your engagement, and are worth reading twice: confidentiality, which continues without limit; the restricted periods in the Code of Conduct; and the record-keeping and reporting duties in the Data Protection and Information Handling Policy at Annex C, sections 4 and 6, which apply to work you have already done.</p>\n    <h2>5 &nbsp;Acknowledgement schedule</h2>\n    <div>\n      <div>I confirm that I have received, read and understood each of the documents listed at section 2, that I have had the opportunity to ask questions about them, and that I accept them as terms of my engagement with Medic Connect. I understand that certain obligations, including confidentiality and the restricted periods in the Code of Conduct, continue after my engagement ends.</div>\n    </div>\n    <div><div>Initial</div></div>\n    <table>\n      <tr>\n        <td>A</td>\n        <td>Code of Conduct</td>\n        <td></td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr>\n        <td>B</td>\n        <td>Confidentiality Policy</td>\n        <td></td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr>\n        <td>C</td>\n        <td>Data Protection and Information Handling</td>\n        <td></td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr>\n        <td>D</td>\n        <td>Scope of Practice Policy</td>\n        <td></td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr>\n        <td>E</td>\n        <td>Disciplinary and Grievance Procedure</td>\n        <td></td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr>\n        <td>F</td>\n        <td>Job description</td>\n        <td></td>\n      </tr>\n    </table>\n    <p>Medic Connect Limited, RC 8026476, 145 Igbosere Road, Lagos Island.</p>",
